---
File-system commands on HopsFS (list, mkdir, upload, download, share,
  remove).

Options:
  --json / --no-json      Force JSON / force human tables (default: JSON when
                          piped).
  --verify / --no-verify  Verify the Hopsworks TLS certificate; --no-verify
                          skips verification for self-signed / IP-SAN-
                          mismatched certs.
  -h, --help              Show this message and exit.

Commands:
  download  Download a file from HopsFS to the local filesystem.
  list      List files under ``path`` in the project's HopsFS.
  mkdir     Create a directory in the project's HopsFS.
  remove    Remove a file or directory from HopsFS.
  share     Share a dataset with another project.
  unshare   Revoke a previously-granted dataset share with another project.
  upload    Upload a local file to HopsFS.
=====FILES UPLOAD=====
Usage: hops files upload [OPTIONS] LOCAL_PATH REMOTE_PATH

  Upload a local file to HopsFS.

  ``REMOTE_PATH`` is the destination path (``cp``/``scp``-style), not the
  parent directory. When its basename matches the local file's basename the
  parent is used as the SDK's ``upload_path``; otherwise the remote path is
  passed through unchanged and the SDK treats it as a directory (file lands
  under ``REMOTE_PATH/<local basename>``).

  Args:     ctx: Click context.     local_path: Local source file.
  remote_path: HopsFS destination path.     overwrite: Pass-through to the
  SDK's upload call.

Options:
  --overwrite             Overwrite an existing remote file.
  --json / --no-json      Force JSON / force human tables (default: JSON when
                          piped).
  --verify / --no-verify  Verify the Hopsworks TLS certificate; --no-verify
                          skips verification for self-signed / IP-SAN-
                          mismatched certs.
  -h, --help              Show this message and exit.
